
============================================================================================
(A) COLLAPSE-vs-IMPROVES: nested LP bounds for CONSEC at each level
============================================================================================
  LP_sym(R)  fixes factorial moments S_1..S_R  (the Delsarte/THM-534 family).
  LP_ind(l)  fixes ALL individual marginals P(A subset M), |A|<=l (relation-code).
  Both -> measS7 at full level (R=6 / l=6).  IMPROVES iff each level strictly drops.

--- k=8 consec, measS7=0.327211 ---
  LP_sym(R): R1=0.73265  R2=0.49637  R3=0.41255  R4=0.35823  R5=0.33252  R6=0.32721
  LP_ind(l): l1=0.66531  l2=0.47925  l3=0.34762  l4=0.32721  l5=0.32721  l6=0.32721
  sym strictly improves R->R+1: [True, True, True, True, True]
  ind strictly improves l->l+1: [True, True, True, False, False]
  level l where LP_ind PINS consec (==measS7): 4
  level R where LP_sym PINS consec (==measS7): 6

--- k=9 consec, measS7=0.416156 ---
