============================================================================================
(B) ARG-MAX TEST: is consec the maximizer of the level-l LP BOUND over shapes?
============================================================================================
  For each shape E the level-l LP bound is a self-upper-bound on measS7(E).
  If consec maximizes the BOUND, a per-level inequality could pin consec.
  We sweep bounded spread; report beaters (shapes whose level-l bound exceeds consec's).

--- k=8 (maxE<=14, 3431 primitive shapes) ---
  measS7(consec)=0.327211; #shapes with HIGHER measS7 = 0 (consec-max truth: True)
  LP_sym(R=1) consec=0.73265  beaters=1  consec-max-of-bound: False
  LP_sym(R=2) consec=0.49637  beaters=0  consec-max-of-bound: True
  LP_sym(R=3) consec=0.41255  beaters=0  consec-max-of-bound: True
  LP_ind(l=1) consec=0.66531  beaters=461  consec-max-of-bound: False
  LP_ind(l=2) consec=0.47925  beaters=0  consec-max-of-bound: True
  LP_ind(l=3) consec=0.34762  beaters=0  consec-max-of-bound: True
  level-2 individual bound argmax: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7] -> 0.47925

--- k=9 (maxE<=12, 495 primitive shapes) ---
  measS7(consec)=0.416156; #shapes with HIGHER measS7 = 0 (consec-max truth: True)
  LP_sym(R=1) consec=0.76978  beaters=10  consec-max-of-bound: False
  LP_sym(R=2) consec=0.56675  beaters=0  consec-max-of-bound: True
  LP_sym(R=3) consec=0.49288  beaters=0  consec-max-of-bound: True
  LP_ind(l=1) consec=0.70680  beaters=101  consec-max-of-bound: False
  LP_ind(l=2) consec=0.55051  beaters=0  consec-max-of-bound: True
  LP_ind(l=3) consec=0.43571  beaters=0  consec-max-of-bound: True
  level-2 individual bound argmax: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8] -> 0.55051

DONE.
